Dear Evans,
I hope you're doing well.
The following are the actions points and recommendations from yesterdays meeting with the bahati team.

- The milk transporters will not be equipped with the POS. This would mean that they'll just have the dairy app in their phones and also the digital scale.
- The transporters should be allowed to take more than one measurement in the case that the quantity of milk delivered is more than the scale can weigh at once.
- Transporters will be the ones to request for feeds and extension services on behalf of the farmers.
- Requests for feeds will be seen by the grader while those ones for vet and clinical services will be viewed by the extension officer. The graders and extension officer can accept or decline these requests.
- There's a new role of a field officer who should be able to register or deregister new transporters. The officer will also be able to dispatch feeds to the graders.
- The graders at the collection centers will be equipped with the platform digital scales so that they can weigh the quantity delivered by the transporters for various routes.
- The graders will be equipped with the POS so that they can issue receipts to the collectors on the quantity they've delivered, the variance and the monthly total.
- Instead of receipts, the farmers will be receiving the usul delivery sms.

The bahati team will communicate with the MD on the same and provide feedback.

Regards,
Michael Ndirangu.